1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Bibi/6000000005380502578 was a silversmith and master craftsman in the Middle East, traveling as far as Bombay for his work. In 1910, he escaped from Beirut to Tunis with his son 
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/people/Reuben-Bibi/6000000000427045674?through=6000000005380502578, and he then went to Lyon for the 1914 World’s Fair. On April 24, 1915, he arrived at Ellis Island, and from there, he went to San Francisco. 
2 CONC He finally settled permanently on the Lower East Side in 1918.
2 CONT
2 CONT For many years, a question was raised as to why Joseph didn’t name any of his children after his parents (https://www.geni.com/people/Abdullah-Bibi/6000000000922753520?through=6000000005380502578 and https://www.geni.com/people/Sa
2 CONC lha-Bibi/6000000002398926370?through=6000000005380502578), as his brother https://www.geni.com/people/Salim-Bibi/6000000109320823251?through=6000000005380502578 had children after them (https://www.geni.com/people/Abdo-Bibi/600000
2 CONC 0109323154833?through=6000000109320823251 and https://www.geni.com/people/Celia-Mizrahi/6000000002703505932). It was later revealed that he had inscribed a Sefer Torah “in memory of his parents, his three brothers: https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Moussa-Bibi/6000000109322286925?through=6000000005380502578, https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bibi/6000000109322283912?through=6000000005380502578, and https://www.geni.com/people/Reuben-Bibi/6000000109322312927?thro
2 CONC ugh=6000000005380502578, and his two sisters https://www.geni.com/people/Bolisa-Bibi/6000000227642406887?through=6000000005380502578 and https://www.geni.com/people/Simha-Bibi/6000000227642517879?through=6000000005380502578". It w
2 CONC as determined from this that he had named his three boys (https://www.geni.com/people/Reuben-Bibi/6000000000427045674?through=6000000005380502578, https://www.geni.com/people/Morris-Bibi/6000000000921879069?through=600000000538050
2 CONC 2578, and https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bibi/6000000000165373240?through=6000000005380502578) after his three brothers who perished in Baghdad, sometime in the 1890s.
