2 CONC 12140828?through=4026171675590010536, and https://www.geni.com/people/Milo-Nakash/6000000075611575153?through=4026171675590010536. However, this is incorrect. https://www.geni.com/people/Sophie-Maslaton/236937?through=402617167559
2 CONC 0010536, https://www.geni.com/people/Rachel-Braha/6000000007282993218?through=4026171675590010536, Adele Cohen (Paris), https://www.geni.com/people/Milo-Nakash/6000000075611575153?through=4026171675590010536, Joseph A. Cohen, and 
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/people/Linda-Tebele/6000000075612140828?through=4026171675590010536 were the children of https://www.geni.com/people/Abraham-Cohen/4026171675590010536 & https://www.geni.com/people/Esther-Cohen/600000007561206
2 CONC 2870?through=4026171675590010536. https://www.geni.com/people/Abraham-Cohen/4026171675590010536 was the eldest son of Joseph & Rachel (Sitt) Cohen. This can be proven from the marriage records of Sophie Maslaton (parents https://w
2 CONC ww.geni.com/people/Abraham-Cohen/4026171675590010536 & Esther Cohen), Rachel Braha (same parents as Sophie), and Linda Tebele (R’ Jacob Kassin’s Ketubah record), although it can easily be assumed, as the spouse of Sophie was named
2 CONC  Joseph, and the father-in-law of Milo was named Yosef, and they assumed that Abraham was a free name. But, Rachel didn't have a Joseph in her family, and as such, she named her son Abraham after her father, https://www.geni.com/p
2 CONC eople/Abraham-Cohen/4026171675590010536. This would make Michel, Moise, Aaron, and the rest of the children of Joseph & Rachel, the aunts and uncles to Sophie, Rachel, and the rest of their family.
